  "source_notes": "Compiled for the 2025-26 NCAA Division III academic year (current as of June 2026). Per task spec, ALL full member institutions of every D3 all-sports conference are listed regardless of whether the school actually sponsors tennis; the men's and women's files are identical full memberships and differ only in the 'gender' field. Sources: Wikipedia 'List of NCAA Division III institutions', 'NCAA Division III', and individual conference articles (en.wikipedia.org); NCAA.com. This covers all 42 D3 all-sports conferences (the Middle Atlantic Conferences are split into their two member leagues, MAC Commonwealth and MAC Freedom, for 43 conference entries total). Notes / uncertainties: (1) Rosters reflect the 2025-26 alignment BEFORE the July 2026 reshuffle (e.g., SUNY New Paltz to NJAC; Alfred State / SUNY Cobleskill / SUNY Delhi to SUNYAC; Luther to Midwest; Maryville & Wesleyan leaving CCS; McMurry & Schreiner back to ASC; Marywood & Neumann to MAC; Saint Francis (PA) to PAC are all 2026-27 changes and are NOT applied here). (2) MASCAC includes Anna Maria for 2025-26 only (the college is closing). (3) Liberty League: 'Rochester' competes as a Liberty League member for sports the UAA doesn't sponsor; Hobart and William Smith are listed as the combined institution 'Hobart and William Smith'. (4) C2C, SCAC, NCAC etc. reflect 2025-26 incoming members (John Carroll in NCAC; Johnson & Wales-Charlotte and Regent in C2C; LeTourneau and returning Hendrix in SCAC). (5) The American Southwest Conference (ASC) has contracted to 4 full members for 2025-26. (6) CUNYAC reflects its eight senior-college (D3) full members. autobid=true for all conferences (each crowns a champion eligible for an NCAA automatic bid). NOTE (D4 carve-out): eighteen academically oriented conferences — NESCAC, Centennial, NCAC, ODAC, SCIAC, SAA, PAC, Landmark, NEWMAC, MIAC, Midwest, Northwest, SCAC, CCS, CCIW, Empire 8, CNE, and C2C — were moved to the new Division IV and are no longer listed here; D3 now holds the remaining 216 full members across 23 conferences.",
